{"command": "cd /testbed && cat > specs/001-transactions/quickstart.md << 'QUICKSTART_EOF'\n# Quickstart Validation Guide: TaggedCache\n\n## Prerequisites\n\n- Python 3.8+ installed\n- Repository cloned at `/testbed`\n- `PYTHONPATH=src:.` for imports\n\n## Validation Scenarios\n\n### S01: Basic Construction and Put/Get\n\n```bash\ncd /testbed\npython3 -c \"\nfrom cachetools.tagged import TaggedCache\nc = TaggedCache(2)\nc.put('a', 1, ['x'])\nassert c.get('a') == 1\nprint('S01 PASS: Basic put/get works')\n\"\n```\n\n**Expected**: Output `S01 PASS: Basic put/get works`\n\n### S02: Tag-Based Invalidation\n\n```bash\ncd /testbed\npython3 -c \"\nfrom cachetools.tagged import TaggedCache\nc = TaggedCache(2)\nc.put('a', 1, ['x'])\nassert c.invalidate('x') == 1\nassert len(c) == 0\nprint('S02 PASS: invalidate returns count and removes entry')\n\"\n```\n\n**Expected**: Output `S02 PASS: invalidate returns count and removes entry`\n\n### S03: Replacement Removes Old Tags\n\n```bash\ncd /testbed\npython3 -c \"\nfrom cachetools.tagged import TaggedCache\nc = TaggedCache(2)\nc.put('a', 1, ['old'])\nc.put('a', 2, ['new'])\nassert c.invalidate('old') == 0\nassert c.get('a') == 2\nprint('S03 PASS: Replacement removes old tag memberships')\n\"\n```\n\n**Expected**: Output `S03 PASS: Replacement removes old tag memberships`\n\n### S04: Deep Copy Isolation\n\n```bash\ncd /testbed\npython3 -c \"\nfrom cachetools.tagged import TaggedCache\nc = TaggedCache(2)\nc.put('a', [1, 2, 3], ['x'])\nresult = c.get('a')\nresult.append(4)\nassert c.get('a') == [1, 2, 3]\nprint('S04 PASS: Deep copy isolation verified')\n\"\n```\n\n**Expected**: Output `S04 PASS: Deep copy isolation verified`\n\n### S05: Input Validation\n\n```bash\ncd /testbed\npython3 -c \"\nfrom cachetools.tagged import TaggedCache\ntry:\n    TaggedCache(maxsize=True)\n    assert False, 'Should have raised ValueError'\nexcept ValueError:\n    pass\ntry:\n    c = TaggedCache(2)\n    c.put('k', 'v', tags='x')\n    assert False, 'Should have raised ValueError'\nexcept ValueError:\n    pass\ntry:\n    c = TaggedCache(2)\n    c.put('k', 'v', tags=[1, 2])\n    assert False, 'Should have raised ValueError'\nexcept ValueError:\n    pass\nprint('S05 PASS: All input validations work')\n\"\n```\n\n**Expected**: Output `S05 PASS: All input validations work`\n\n### S06: LRU Eviction with Tag Cleanup\n\n```bash\ncd /testbed\npython3 -c \"\nfrom cachetools.tagged import TaggedCache\nc = TaggedCache(2)\nc.put('a', 1, ['x'])\nc.put('b', 2, ['y'])\nc.get('a')  # refresh recency of 'a'\nc.put('c', 3, ['z'])  # should evict 'b'\nassert 'b' not in c\nassert c.get('a') == 1\nassert c.get('c') == 3\nassert c.invalidate('y') == 0  # 'b' was evicted, not invalidated\nprint('S06 PASS: LRU eviction cleans up tag indexes')\n\"\n```\n\n**Expected**: Output `S06 PASS: LRU eviction cleans up tag indexes`\n\n### S07: Public Acceptance Tests\n\n```bash\ncd /testbed\npython3 -m pytest acceptance_public.py -v\n```\n\n**Expected**: All tests pass.\n\n### S08: Upstream Tests\n\n```bash\ncd /testbed\npython3 -m pytest tests/ -v\n```\n\n**Expected**: All upstream tests pass.\n\n## Notes\n\n- Each scenario is independently verifiable.\n- S07 and S08 are the final acceptance gates.\n- If any scenario fails, the implementation has a bug.\nQUICKSTART_EOF", "exit_code": 0, "stderr": "", "stdout": ""}